<title>MEXICO: Mexico avocado growers cautiously eye U.S. exports.</title>
<headline>Mexico avocado growers cautiously eye U.S. exports.</headline>
<byline>Chris Aspin</byline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican avocado growers said on Monday they were taking a more level-headed stance to the lifting of an 83-year U.S. ban on the exports of avocadoes than the fanfare victory trumpeted by the Mexican government.</p>
<p>The opening could mean just 5,000 tonnes of Mexican avocadoes enter the U.S. market each winter because of the strict limitations still in place and transport distances.</p>
<p>The United States said Friday its export ban was lifted in 19 U.S. states between November and February each year.</p>
</text>
